O1: stack-name prefix and a dedicated CDK bootstrap (FAST Channels overlay on the guidance v1.4.0)

The shipped app hard-codes its stack names and synthesizes for the default bootstrap qualifier (hnb659fds), whose
CloudFormation execution role is often AdministratorAccess. New, optional CDK context values (unset: the app
synthesizes exactly as shipped):
  stackPrefix                 stack names <stackPrefix>-pbs and <stackPrefix>-pbs-sim; construct ids are unchanged
  bootstrapQualifier          a dedicated bootstrap's qualifier, for both stacks
  fileAssetsBucketName        that bootstrap's file assets bucket
  imageAssetsRepositoryName   that bootstrap's container assets repository
CloudFormation parameters are keyed by stack name, so with a prefix pass them as <stackPrefix>-pbs:<Name>=<value>.
With a prefix the MetricsEtl Glue database is named <stackPrefix>-prebid-server-<region>-metricsetl-database: the
shipped name is the guidance's only name unique per account and Region that does not depend on the stack, so two
prefixed deployments in one account and Region collided on it.

